# Required
QERTUM_IMAGE=registry.example.lan:5000/qertum-services:latest
# The public name users type in the browser, exactly (no NAT, DNS alias or other name in between):
# sign-in accepts only this address, and every container must resolve it.
QERTUM_HOST=ca.example.lan
QERTUM_EST_TLS_CERT=/etc/qertum/est/tls.crt
QERTUM_EST_TLS_KEY=/etc/qertum/est/tls.key

# Browser/API: configure the TLS proxy described in README before starting.
QERTUM_SCHEME=https
QERTUM_TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# Optional
# QERTUM_DATA=/mnt/user/appdata/qertum   # existing host path: also add docker-compose.bind.yml
# QERTUM_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1          # default; keep plaintext backend ports private
# QERTUM_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=true       # isolated HTTP lab only; also QERTUM_SCHEME=http and reachable bind address
# QERTUM_SCHEME=https                    # when a proxy terminates TLS for web, identity and api (never acme or est)
# QERTUM_TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.18.0.0/16   # required with QERTUM_SCHEME=https: the proxy's IP or network (comma-separated)
# ACME_SCHEME=https                      # only when the acme container terminates TLS itself (see README)
# SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# TPM_DEVICE=/dev/tpmrm0
# TPM_GROUP=105
